    },
    {
      "id": "tMilpjPVYFJgE3xflbfBE",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 531.7057142485874,
      "y": 2088.4196343064223,
      "width": 1132.559326171875,
      "height": 120,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJh",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 425871808,
      "version": 977,
      "versionNonce": 430051776,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1762801374660,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- The app will have an offline first approach, to have faster load times, reduce data usage and work well offline. \n- Users can browse their complete existing collection of recipes and meal plans fully offline\n- Users can add recipes and generate meal plans while offline that will be synced with the BE upon reconnection. \n- SQLite will be used as the data is relational, we will benefit from ACID transactions, and compex queries, can set up FTS\n- Main Access Patterns: getRecipes, getMeal plans. Those will involve joins to put them together. Can use a materialized view to speed up joins. \n- All entities will have a a creatorId, updatedAt, deletedAt, updatedByClientId, syncStatus.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- The app will have an offline first approach, to have faster load times, reduce data usage and work well offline. \n- Users can browse their complete existing collection of recipes and meal plans fully offline\n- Users can add recipes and generate meal plans while offline that will be synced with the BE upon reconnection. \n- SQLite will be used as the data is relational, we will benefit from ACID transactions, and compex queries, can set up FTS\n- Main Access Patterns: getRecipes, getMeal plans. Those will involve joins to put them together. Can use a materialized view to speed up joins. \n- All entities will have a a creatorId, updatedAt, deletedAt, updatedByClientId, syncStatus.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "iZ0ba-TDNJb4Dhpe0rsE3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 525.9788239854901,
      "y": 2232.0982069493075,
      "width": 804.4004516601562,
      "height": 240,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJj",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 471732672,
      "version": 203,
      "versionNonce": 2038804928,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1762793966140,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "| Entity                                      | Description                                              |\n| ------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `UserEntity`                                | Creator/owner of recipes                                 |\n| `RecipeEntity`                              | Updated: prepTime, cookTime, servings, creatorId FK      |\n| `TagEntity` / `LabelEntity`                 | Tagging + labeling system                                |\n| `RecipeTagCrossRef` / `RecipeLabelCrossRef` | Many-to-many joins                                       |\n| `GenericIngredientEntity`                   | Master list of ingredients (almonds, minced meat, etc.)  |\n| `AllergenEntity`                            | Defines allergens (nuts, gluten, shellfish, etc.)        |\n| `SourceClassificationEntity`                | Defines ingredient origins (animal, vegetal, fish, etc.) |\n| `RecipeIngredientEntity`                    | Links recipes to generic ingredients + quantities        |\n| `RecipeStepEntity`                          | Unchanged (still recipe-specific)                        |\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "| Entity                                      | Description                                              |\n| ------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `UserEntity`                                | Creator/owner of recipes                                 |\n| `RecipeEntity`                              | Updated: prepTime, cookTime, servings, creatorId FK      |\n| `TagEntity` / `LabelEntity`                 | Tagging + labeling system                                |\n| `RecipeTagCrossRef` / `RecipeLabelCrossRef` | Many-to-many joins                                       |\n| `GenericIngredientEntity`                   | Master list of ingredients (almonds, minced meat, etc.)  |\n| `AllergenEntity`                            | Defines allergens (nuts, gluten, shellfish, etc.)        |\n| `SourceClassificationEntity`                | Defines ingredient origins (animal, vegetal, fish, etc.) |\n| `RecipeIngredientEntity`                    | Links recipes to generic ingredients + quantities        |\n| `RecipeStepEntity`                          | Unchanged (still recipe-specific)                        |\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TodYQOMdCSVdWle1n442E",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1712.4292755711363,
      "y": 2186.653889430003,
      "width": 1919.5950927734375,
      "height": 945,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJm",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2051725760,
      "version": 1483,
      "versionNonce": 1430596032,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1762801819432,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Syncing changes between BE and Clients\n- A recipe on average has about 3500 charactets. At one byte per char that is a 3.5KB payload. \nSyncing:\n- when: on app start up -> Workmanager\n- when (nice to have): when phone charging and on wifi networks. -> Broadcast reciever? + Workmanager\n- when making an update locally (eg. adding / editing recipe)\n- when: FCM push notification on BE changes (out of scope for now)\n- how: we don't want to fech data that is already up to date.\n    - keep track of revision history on a  grouping multiple changes. Each revision has an id associated\n    along with a changeset. Each id keeps the lastest changes. eg. for recipes. add recipe(id), editRecipeId(i), editIngredientCrossRef(id, id)\n    More complex but should minimize payload and be fast as it's generated on the BE on writes.  The changes will be \n    grouped by entityType. \n- Network DS for each repo will contain methods for syncing eg.\ninterface RecipeRemoteDataSource {\n    suspend fun pushChanges(changes: SyncPayload): ApiResponse\n    suspend fun pullChanges(since: Long): SyncResponse\n} \n\n| Problem                  | Solution                                                           |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Detect out-of-sync       | Compare timestamps (per Entity) (`updatedAt`, `deletedAt`) since `lastSyncedAt` and Sync State |\n| Efficient delta transfer | Send only changed entities grouped by type                         |\n| Conflict handling        | Last-writer-wins for now                                           |\n| Local queue for writes   | Use an Outbox table                                                |\n| Sortable, safe IDs       | UUIDv7 / ULID (backend generated)                                  |\n| Sync trigger             | WorkManager on startup / connectivity / user edits                 |\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Syncing changes between BE and Clients\n- A recipe on average has about 3500 charactets. At one byte per char that is a 3.5KB payload. \nSyncing:\n- when: on app start up -> Workmanager\n- when (nice to have): when phone charging and on wifi networks. -> Broadcast reciever? + Workmanager\n- when making an update locally (eg. adding / editing recipe)\n- when: FCM push notification on BE changes (out of scope for now)\n- how: we don't want to fech data that is already up to date.\n    - keep track of revision history on a  grouping multiple changes. Each revision has an id associated\n    along with a changeset. Each id keeps the lastest changes. eg. for recipes. add recipe(id), editRecipeId(i), editIngredientCrossRef(id, id)\n    More complex but should minimize payload and be fast as it's generated on the BE on writes.  The changes will be \n    grouped by entityType. \n- Network DS for each repo will contain methods for syncing eg.\ninterface RecipeRemoteDataSource {\n    suspend fun pushChanges(changes: SyncPayload): ApiResponse\n    suspend fun pullChanges(since: Long): SyncResponse\n} \n\n| Problem                  | Solution                                                           |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Detect out-of-sync       | Compare timestamps (per Entity) (`updatedAt`, `deletedAt`) since `lastSyncedAt` and Sync State |\n| Efficient delta transfer | Send only changed entities grouped by type                         |\n| Conflict handling        | Last-writer-wins for now                                           |\n| Local queue for writes   | Use an Outbox table                                                |\n| Sortable, safe IDs       | UUIDv7 / ULID (backend generated)                                  |\n| Sync trigger             | WorkManager on startup / connectivity / user edits                 |\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Pl-r1oFPd3q6bevwVV5Mz",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1234.7470088757009,
      "y": 1275.4815125904279,
      "width": 693.7323959000279,
      "height": 966.9475628429177,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 768520640,
      "version": 226,
      "versionNonce": 1368535488,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1762800965872,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "// Enpoints below are optional, as all changes will flow via the sync API\n\nPOST /recipes/v1/recipe\nPostRecipeReq(\n    reqId, // idemp key\n    Recipe\n)\nResponse: 201 Created \nPostRecipeResp(\n     recipeId, // BE generated\n)\n\nPUT /recipes/v1/recipe/<id>\nPostRecipeReq(\n    reqId, // idemp key\n    Recipe\n)\n\nDELETE  /recipes/v1/recipe/<id>\n\nGET /recipes/v1/recipe/<id>\nResponse: 200\nGetRecipeResponse(\n      RecipeDetails\n)\n\n\n// The following endpoints might not be needed if we pull from local DB and sync with the BE. \n\nGET /recipes/v1/recipes?page=<>limit=<>\nResponse: 200\nGetRecipesResponse(\n    pagingMeta,\n    List<RecipePreview>\n)\n\n// This might not be needed if we generate on the BE.\nGET /mealplans/v1/generate\nResponse: 200\nGenMealPlanResponse(\n    mealPlanId,\n    mealPlanTitle,\n    labels,\n    List<Recipes>\n)\n\nGET /mealplans/v1/mealplans\nResponse: 200\nGetMealPlansResponse(\n    List<MealPlans>\n    List<MealPlans> cooked.\n)",
      "fontSize": 14.876116351429507,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "// Enpoints below are optional, as all changes will flow via the sync API\n\nPOST /recipes/v1/recipe\nPostRecipeReq(\n    reqId, // idemp key\n    Recipe\n)\nResponse: 201 Created \nPostRecipeResp(\n     recipeId, // BE generated\n)\n\nPUT /recipes/v1/recipe/<id>\nPostRecipeReq(\n    reqId, // idemp key\n    Recipe\n)\n\nDELETE  /recipes/v1/recipe/<id>\n\nGET /recipes/v1/recipe/<id>\nResponse: 200\nGetRecipeResponse(\n      RecipeDetails\n)\n\n\n// The following endpoints might not be needed if we pull from local DB and sync with the BE. \n\nGET /recipes/v1/recipes?page=<>limit=<>\nResponse: 200\nGetRecipesResponse(\n    pagingMeta,\n    List<RecipePreview>\n)\n\n// This might not be needed if we generate on the BE.\nGET /mealplans/v1/generate\nResponse: 200\nGenMealPlanResponse(\n    mealPlanId,\n    mealPlanTitle,\n    labels,\n    List<Recipes>\n)\n\nGET /mealplans/v1/mealplans\nResponse: 200\nGetMealPlansResponse(\n    List<MealPlans>\n    List<MealPlans> cooked.\n)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
